From 5b4953bebee674dff661eb5b35bb81a8ee63d423 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Robson <danny19901@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:58:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] feat(ui): gamepad navigation for ImGui overlays and app
 input blocking

SDL gamepad button and axis events reached the windowed app context and
were dropped, so overlays could only be used with a keyboard and mouse.

- Add GamepadEvent and WindowInputListener::OnGamepadEvent. The SDL app
  context forwards SDL_EVENT_GAMEPAD_* to every window (gamepads are not
  tied to one), and WindowSDL translates buttons and axes.
- ImGuiDrawer maps them onto ImGui's gamepad keys (with a stick dead zone)
  and enables ImGuiConfigFlags_NavEnableGamepad, so every dialog, including
  the F4 settings editor, can be driven with a controller.
- Add ReXApp::IsGuestInputBlocked, consulted by the input active callback,
  so an app's own overlay can keep the guest from seeing the controller
  while it is open. The SDK only knew about its own overlays before.

Guest input is unaffected: the input drivers still read gamepads through
their own event watch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
